      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure thing, I can do better here to match the mix of ethnicities and come up with younger or less established characters in your south side setting.\n\n1. **Jamal \"Mint\" Rodriguez**: Seventeen, new on the streets, Jamal has that cruel streak from seeing what's been through his neighborhood, but it's also a burning determination to make something of himself. With a laid-back swagger, he swings his leather messenger bag over his shoulder, hiding a pocket full of his mom's homemade pastries. Jamal's fresh but tired smile can disappear into a faraway look—the telltale sign of someone who's quick to lose hope but not to keep moving.\n\n2. **Elena \"Pixie\" Mendoza**: At sixteen, she's a kid who's seen too much and never really known a calm moment. Elena a small but swiftly growing girl of mixed heritage, sporting a long braid of her Fair Colombian hair, covered in Elmore Street's harsh realities. She wears borrowed jeans, muddy tracks on her shoes that lead to haphazardly holey bills. Despite it all, she shows a light in her small brown eyes, a gratitude for the few fights she’s won instead of the losses piled high.\n\n3. **Kofi",
